/* psp5 authentic - the curves of the moving shapes of PS3 and PS4 (see theme.c). Header-only: it is included by theme.c and nothing else.
 *
 * Both were measured from the maintainer's reference animations (8 s, 15 images a second), then smoothed and reduced to a few numbers:
 *
 * PS3, the ribbon: three curves (its upper edge, its lower edge and its bright strand), each a sum of MX smooth waves along the screen (cosines)
 * whose heights move with the loop (a constant and NH sine/cosine pairs of the period). The reference jumps where it loops, so its last two
 * seconds were blended into its first two before the fit: the loop is 6 s and has no seam. Values are screen pixels (480 x 272).
 *
 * PS4, the wave: PS4N_K keys of the wave, each PS4N_J points from the bottom of the screen up to its top right corner: where the point is (x, y in
 * tenths of a pixel), how bright the edge is (ae) and how bright the soft band at its left is (bb), both as alpha 0-255 times two.
 * The tracking was repaired at the two ends of the wave afterwards (docs/DEVELOPER-NOTES.md): where the reference has faded at the bottom of the screen the lowest
 * two points of keys 17 to 29 had wandered (their steps turned flat, so that the strip folded over itself), and the last point of every key was pinned to the top
 * right corner (a 40 to 66 degree turn in the last step, which folds the strip there). Each of these steps was clamped to a smooth continuation of the curve
 * (the bottom ones: to lean at most 14 degrees less than the step above and at most 2 more, never past straight up, at most 23 px long; the last one: to turn
 * at most 12 degrees from the step before it); a step that was already inside those limits is as it was measured. The values of ae and bb are as measured. */
